{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ImplicitScalar","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ImplicitScalar","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.InverseFunctionTheorem.FDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Comp","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Pow","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Add","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.exists_sqrt_branch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.exists_sqrt_branch","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ImplicitScalar.lean#L189-L209","doc":"**Usability check.** An existence theorem whose hypotheses nothing satisfies\nis worthless, so here it is instantiated end to end on `f (x,y) = y² − x` at\n`(1,1)`: `∂f/∂y = 2 ≠ 0`, `∂f/∂x = −1`, and the theorem returns a branch of\n`√x` through `1` with `g′(1) = −(−1)/2 = 1/2` — the derivative of `√x` at `1`,\nas it must be. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.exists_hasDerivAt_implicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.exists_hasDerivAt_implicit","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ImplicitScalar.lean#L118-L185","doc":"**Scalar implicit function theorem.**\n\nIf `f : 𝕜 × 𝕜 → 𝕜` is strictly differentiable at `(x₀, y₀)`, vanishes there, and\nits `y`-partial `B := f' (0,1)` is nonzero, then there is a function `g` with\n`g x₀ = y₀`, solving `f (x, g x) = 0` near `x₀`, and\n\n    g' x₀ = −A / B,     A := f' (1,0).\n\nProved by straightening the graph with `(x,y) ↦ (x, f (x,y))` and applying\nMathlib's inverse function theorem, rather than through `ImplicitFunctionData`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.straightenEquiv_symm_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.straightenEquiv_symm_apply","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ImplicitScalar.lean#L112-L114","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.straightenEquiv_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.straightenEquiv_apply","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ImplicitScalar.lean#L109-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.straightenEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.straightenEquiv","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ImplicitScalar.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**The straightening map is a linear equivalence exactly when `∂f/∂y ≠ 0`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.unstraighten_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.unstraighten_apply","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ImplicitScalar.lean#L95-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.unstraighten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.unstraighten","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ImplicitScalar.lean#L90-L93","doc":"The inverse: `(a,b) ↦ (a, (b − A·a)/B)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.straighten_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.straighten_apply","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ImplicitScalar.lean#L86-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.straighten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.straighten","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ImplicitScalar.lean#L81-L84","doc":"`L A B (a,b) = (a, A·a + B·b)` — the derivative of `(x,y) ↦ (x, f x y)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}